segs:[
 {tag:'段 1 · 定义', h:'先说它是什么、在哪儿、赚什么',
  p:['“Glycolysis is a process, a sequence of enzyme-catalysed reactions in the cytosol. It converts one glucose into two pyruvate, with a net gain of two ATP and two NADH. The cytosol is the soluble part of the cytoplasm outside the organelles. Pyruvate is the three-carbon 2-oxo acid. The textbook’s definition is one sentence: the sequence of reactions by which glucose is converted to pyruvate with simultaneous production of ATP. No step uses oxygen, and it is almost universal — the same reactions in nearly all organisms and all cell types.”',
     '“It is a catabolic pathway — a breakdown route that releases energy. And it is the common trunk of carbohydrate catabolism: glycogen, galactose and fructose all enter it, and pyruvate is the branch point. With oxygen, pyruvate goes into the mitochondrion and is oxidised completely. In a working muscle short of oxygen it is temporarily reduced to lactate. In yeast it goes to ethanol.”'],
  note:'<b>「胞质」「丙酮酸」「分解代谢」三个词都在同一句里交代了</b>——它们承重。三个去向是 p164 第一段的顺序。'},
 {tag:'段 2 · general', h:'先给账和形状，再给步骤',
  p:['“The balance per glucose: two ATP invested at the two hexose phosphorylations, four made at the two substrate-level phosphorylations, so the net gain is two ATP. Add two NADH from the one oxidation, and two pyruvate. Glucose is not oxidised to CO₂. All six carbons are still there.”',
     '“The pathway has two halves. The first five reactions invest two ATP to turn one six-carbon sugar into two three-carbon phosphates. The last five oxidise each triose once and harvest four ATP. Three of the ten steps are practically irreversible: hexokinase, phosphofructokinase and pyruvate kinase. The textbook singles out phosphofructokinase as the rate-limiting, allosterically controlled step.”'],
  note:'<b>先给净账和三个不可逆步，再给十步</b>。直接背十步是 technician 的答法；先说「四造二投、三步不可逆、PFK 控制」，他就知道你理解了形状。'},
 {tag:'段 3 · 稍展开', h:'十步，每步只给「谁变成谁 ＋ 酶」，然后 NAD⁺ 问题',
  p:['“Hexokinase, or glucokinase in the liver, phosphorylates glucose at C-6 with ATP. Hexose phosphate isomerase converts the aldose to the ketose, fructose-6-phosphate. Phosphofructokinase adds the second ATP at C-1, giving fructose-1,6-bisphosphate. Aldolase splits it into dihydroxyacetone phosphate and glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate. And triose phosphate isomerase interconverts them, so we have two glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate.”',
     '“Then, twice. Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase oxidises the aldehyde with NAD-plus and takes up inorganic phosphate, giving 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate — an acyl phosphate, macroergic. Phosphoglycerate kinase hands that phosphate to ADP — substrate-level phosphorylation, the first ATP. Phosphoglycerate mutase moves the remaining phosphate from C-3 to C-2. Enolase removes water to give phosphoenolpyruvate — an enol phosphate, the highest free energy of hydrolysis in the textbook’s table. And pyruvate kinase hands that to ADP, the second ATP, giving pyruvate.”',
     '“The one thing that ties it to oxygen is NAD-plus. The dehydrogenase needs it, the pool is small, and the textbook says that if NADH were not reoxidised the pathway could not go beyond glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate. Without oxygen pyruvate is the acceptor — lactate dehydrogenase in muscle, pyruvate decarboxylase and alcohol dehydrogenase in yeast. With oxygen the respiratory chain reoxidises it, and the yield goes from two ATP to the textbook’s thirty-eight.”'],
  note:'<b>时间不够就砍到三句</b>：五步投资到两个 GAP；五步收获——一次氧化、两次底物水平磷酸化；NAD⁺ 必须再生。<b>「NAD⁺ 问题」那一句不要砍</b>，它是 anaerobic 这个词的全部内容。'},
 {tag:'段 4 · 留口子', h:'落到酵母和你量的东西',
  p:['“One thing worth adding from my own work: the organism I use every day is yeast, and it runs exactly this pathway. It is the textbook’s example of a facultative anaerobe, so in glucose it ferments to ethanol. And when I move the cells to galactose to induce my display construct, the sugar enters glycolysis through galactokinase, the uridyltransferase and UDP-glucose-4-epimerase. That is the same page of the textbook. And two of these enzymes are the textbook’s standard cases of what I have to think about when I measure binding. Phosphofructokinase stands for allosteric control, and lactate dehydrogenase has five isoenzymes that catalyse the same reaction with different kinetics. The same protein family, different constants — and that is exactly the kind of difference I measure as a dissociation constant.”'],
  note:'口子落在 <b>卡 02（Kd）</b> 和大本营卡。酵母兼性厌氧 p016；半乳糖三个酶 p172；LDH 同工酶 p064–p065；PFK 变构 p164。<b>Crabtree 效应和 GAL 启动子的葡萄糖阻遏是通用知识</b>，被追问时说成自己的，不说成书的。<b>不点病原体的名字。</b>'}
],

why:{
 rungs:[
  ['为什么不需要氧也能造 ATP？','因为<b>醛氧化成酸</b>那一步（GAPDH）本身是强放能的，而且书说它<b>跟吸进无机磷酸偶联</b>——能量没变成热，先存进硫酯、再存进<b>酰基磷酸</b>（−49.3），比 ATP（−30.5）高，所以能把磷酸转给 ADP。电子受体是 <b>NAD⁺</b>，不是氧。'],
  ['那为什么只有 2 个？','因为葡萄糖<b>没有被氧化</b>——六个碳原样在两个丙酮酸里，每个三碳糖只氧化了一次（醛 → 羧酸）。书的数：到乳酸只放出 −196.6，完全氧化 −2870。而且那两对电子（NADH）无氧时还得<b>还回给丙酮酸</b>才能继续，所以氧化那一步的收益等于零。'],
  ['为什么不把 NADH 留着？','因为 NAD⁺ 是一个<b>催化量的池子</b>，很小。没有受体（有氧时是呼吸链、无氧时是丙酮酸）几秒钟就全变成 NADH，GAPDH 就停——书 p168 原话：不再生 NAD⁺，糖酵解走不过 GAP，ATP 既造不出也再生不了。']
 ],
 stop:{lbl:'停 · 落在热力学',
  say:'“Below that we are asking why an acyl phosphate or an enol phosphate holds more free energy than a phosphoanhydride. The answer is resonance and charge repulsion, which is physical chemistry rather than biochemistry.”'}
},

